Ah — classic print issue. The visibility: hidden approach hides content but the elements still occupy space in the page flow, so the browser generates empty pages for all the rest of the document. The fix is to switch from visibility to display: none on everything, then explicitly display: block (or appropriate) on just the checklist and its heading. That removes the hidden content from the layout entirely, so no trailing blank pages.

Replace the previous @media print block with this one:

```css
/* ---------- PRINT: CHECKLIST ONLY ---------- */
@media print {
  /* Remove everything from layout flow */
  body > * {
    display: none !important;
  }

  /* Reveal the ancestor chain of the checklist */
  body > .container,
  body > .container > #field-techniques {
    display: block !important;
  }

  /* Hide everything inside the section except the checklist */
  #field-techniques > * {
    display: none !important;
  }

  #field-techniques > h3:nth-of-type(2) {   /* "Field Kit Checklist" heading */
    display: block !important;
  }

  #field-techniques > .checklist {
    display: block !important;
  }

  /* Reset page margins & colours for print */
  body {
    background: #fff !important;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .container {
    max-width: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  #field-techniques {
    box-shadow: none !important;
    border: none !important;
    border-radius: 0 !important;
    padding: 0 !important;
    margin: 0 !important;
  }

  /* Print-friendly title above the list */
  .checklist::before {
    content: "Field Kit Checklist — CIII CEM";
    display: block;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #1e3a1e;
    border-bottom: 3px solid #e6b422;
    padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  }

  /* Each item as a clean line with a visible empty box */
  .checklist-item {
    display: flex !important;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    padding: 0.35rem 0;
    background: none;
    border-bottom: 1px dotted #bbb;
    page-break-inside: avoid;
  }

  .checklist-item input[type="checkbox"] {
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    accent-color: #000;
  }

  .checklist-item label {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #000;
  }

  /* Hide the print button */
  .print-btn {
    display: none !important;
  }

  /* Prevent blank pages from stray margins */
  html, body {
    height: auto !important;
    overflow: visible !important;
  }
}
```

---

Why the previous version leaked pages

visibility: hidden keeps the element's box in the layout — so all your sections, cards, footer, etc. still reserved their full height on the page, producing blank pages 2–8. display: none removes them from the flow entirely, so only the checklist's real height is printed.

What this version does

1. body > * → display: none kills the hero, nav, footer, and every section in one hit.
2. Then it re-reveals only the chain needed: .container → #field-techniques → its checklist heading and the checklist itself.
3. Everything else inside #field-techniques (the card grids, essential skills, etc.) stays hidden.
4. Section padding, margins, shadows, and border-radius are stripped so the checklist starts at the top of the page and the page fits cleanly.
5. html, body { height: auto; overflow: visible; } prevents the sticky nav's fixed positioning from creating an extra tall page.

One thing to verify

The selector #field-techniques > h3:nth-of-type(2) targets the "Field Kit Checklist" heading specifically — but only if that heading is a direct child of the section and is the second <h3> in it. In your current markup, the structure is:

```html
<section id="field-techniques">
  <h2>Field Techniques…</h2>
  <h3>Essential Skills for CIII CEM</h3>   <!-- 1st h3 -->
  <div class="card-container">…</div>
  <h3>Field Kit Checklist</h3>             <!-- 2nd h3 -->
  <div class="checklist">…</div>
  <button class="print-btn">…</button>
</section>
```

So h3:nth-of-type(2) is correct. If you ever add or reorder headings, adjust that number — or, cleaner, give the heading an id (e.g. id="checklist-heading") and target #checklist-heading instead. That would be the more robust long-term fix; happy to swap it in if you'd like.

Test it once with Print Preview rather than actually printing — that'll show you immediately whether the page count is now 1 (or 2, depending on checklist length) instead of 9.
